body:
### Tested versions

v4.5.stable.official [876b29033]

### System information

Godot v4.5.stable - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1060 3GB (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.7247) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-6400 CPU @ 2.70GHz (4 threads) - 15.95 GiB memory

### Issue description

`Image.compress(Image.COMPRESS_BPTC)` and `PortableCompressedTexture2D.create_from_image(Image, PortableCompressedTexture2D.COMPRESSION_MODE_BPTC)` both fail in the exported builds.

My game has ability to heavily customize the player's skin. This relies on ability to generate textures in-runtime. Without compression, 2k textures end up using 32mb of VRAM per player. With compression, this goes down to 4mb. But it seems to be impossible to get compression working in the exported builds currently

From my quick glance, the culprit seems to be here but I might be wrong:
https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/b4472f4670a0b7fd34137d18f1e080e3319e3819/modules/cvtt/register_types.cpp#L33

`#ifdef TOOLS_ENABLED` makes it so these functions are only defined in the editor build. It'd be great if this functionality was accessible in the exported builds too

### Steps to reproduce

https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/054791c1-c57c-4f0e-99a2-6754258e5061

This code is enough to trigger the issue. Works fine in the editor build, fails when running from an exported build (the MRP has a logger built-in that shows well)

```
func _ready() -> void:
	compressPortable()
	compressImage()

const ICON = preload("res://icon.svg")

func compressPortable():
	var IconImage := ICON.get_image()
	var portableCompressedTexture = PortableCompressedTexture2D.new()
	portableCompressedTexture.create_from_image(IconImage, PortableCompressedTexture2D.COMPRESSION_MODE_BPTC)

	if(portableCompressedTexture.get_format() == Image.FORMAT_BPTC_RGBA):
		print("compressPortable(): Success, Format="+str(portableCompressedTexture.get_format())+", Compression mode="+str(portableCompressedTexture.get_compression_mode()))
	else:
		print("compressPortable(): Failed, Format="+str(portableCompressedTexture.get_format())+", Compression mode="+str(portableCompressedTexture.get_compression_mode()))

func compressImage():
	var IconImage := ICON.get_image()
	IconImage.compress(Image.COMPRESS_BPTC)

	if(IconImage.get_format() == Image.FORMAT_BPTC_RGBA):
		print("compressImage(): Success, Format="+str(IconImage.get_format()))
	else:
		print("compressImage(): Failed, Format="+str(IconImage.get_format()))
```

